{
  "version": 8,
  "description": "Curated city + island/natural-landmark reference list for the Earth city-label layer (UX-11 #5). Offline-first; lat/lon in degrees. NAME POLICY: no abbreviations, no jargon, ASCII only, <= 22 characters (Strait not Str, Mountains not Mts, Island(s) not Is, Mount not Mt, Saint not St; parentheses/hyphens allowed). KIND: city = a populated place; landmark = island, archipelago, range, desert, sea, gulf, delta, plateau, reef, ice sheet, trench, pole; launch = pad or range; strait = strait, canal, channel, passage, cape. TIER: 1 = school-atlas recognisable, ALL launch sites, isolated ocean/polar references; 2 = regionally recognisable; 3 = dense-cluster secondary, close zoom only. PIN: optional 'pin': true forces a label past BOTH the zoom LOD gate and screen-space declutter — it is placed before every other label, including launch pads, and ignores the maxVisible budgets. Use sparingly (each pinned label costs a slot from the curated set at far zoom); intended for entries that must always be findable regardless of recognition. BUDGET: one in, one out — the file stays <= 405 so MAX_CITIES (420) keeps headroom; a new entry retires one of equal or lower recognition. KEEP-CRITERIA (any one suffices): (a) recognition — a non-local would know the name; (b) coverage criticality — in view during stretches with <= 5 labels; (c) corridor landfall — marks where a track crosses from ocean onto land (e.g. Visakhapatnam).",
